PUBLIC_WRITING_SNAPSHOT = tuple(json.loads(r'''[{"slug":"secure-enterprise-ai-ten-failures-to-control","title":"Secure Enterprise AI: The Ten Failures Executives Must Be Ready to Control","deck":"The executive test is not whether AI works in a demonstration. It is whether the organisation can prove what the system may see, say and do—and contain failure.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"Enterprise AI Security & Reliability","read_minutes":8,"published_label":"02 Nov 2026"},{"slug":"data-governance-vs-ai-governance-executive-decisions","title":"Data Governance vs AI Governance: Two Controls, One Business Decision","deck":"Data governance establishes whether information can be trusted and used. AI governance decides whether an AI-enabled workflow should be allowed to act—and who owns the consequences.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"AI & Data Governance","read_minutes":8,"published_label":"02 Nov 2026"},{"slug":"data-governance-what-deserves-funding","title":"Data Governance: What Deserves Funding?","deck":"Stop selling a governance programme. Show the operating failure, the control that changes it, and the proof needed to invest further.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"AI & Data Governance","read_minutes":6,"published_label":"02 Nov 2026"},{"slug":"eu-ai-act-what-executives-must-decide","title":"EU AI Act: What Executives Must Decide Now","deck":"Know which AI uses are prohibited, which trigger specific duties, who is responsible and what evidence is needed before approval.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"EU AI Act & AI Governance","read_minutes":7,"published_label":"02 Nov 2026"},{"slug":"ai-governance-explained-to-executives","title":"AI Governance Explained to Executives","deck":"Seven governance layers, one business example and a six-field decision record to help leaders decide when AI is ready for controlled use.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"AI & Data Governance","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"01 Nov 2026"},{"slug":"seven-questions-for-better-ai-decisions","title":"Seven Questions for Better AI Decisions","deck":"An executive field guide to challenging AI proposals, strengthening ownership and moving from promising demos to defensible decisions.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"AI Leadership & Decision Quality","read_minutes":5,"published_label":"31 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-capabilities-executive-decisions","title":"AI, ML, GenAI, RAG and Agents: What Executives Actually Need to Know","deck":"A practical guide to choosing the right AI capability for a business process, setting boundaries around autonomy and measuring whether the work improves.","kind":"Executive Briefing","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":7,"published_label":"31 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"when-your-best-people-disagree-with-the-ai","title":"When Your Best People Disagree with the AI","deck":"An experienced employee rejecting an AI recommendation may be protecting the business—or protecting an old habit. Leadership needs a way to tell the difference.","kind":"Article","category":"AI Adoption","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"25 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"the-ai-innovation-future-i-see-from-gothenburg","title":"The AI Innovation Future I See from Gothenburg","deck":"Sweden is one of the world’s leading countries for innovation. Living and working in Gothenburg, I have plenty of reasons to be proud of that. But my experience leading AI initiatives has also taught me that having great ideas and making them work are two very different things.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Innovation","read_minutes":7,"published_label":"24 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-can-make-every-team-faster-and-still-leave-the-business-slow","title":"AI Can Make Every Team Faster and Still Leave the Business Slow","deck":"AI can improve individual productivity without improving the performance of the business. If faster work simply creates larger queues, more hand-offs or new bottlenecks elsewhere, the organization has automated activity rather than improved flow.","kind":"Article","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"18 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"if-ai-does-the-routine-work-how-will-we-develop-the-next-experts","title":"If AI Does the Routine Work, How Will We Develop the Next Experts?","deck":"As AI takes on more everyday tasks, organizations can improve performance while changing how employees gain experience. The challenge is to capture those gains without weakening the expertise needed when technology reaches its limits.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-is-turning-data-definitions-into-a-leadership-problem","title":"AI Is Turning Data Definitions Into a Leadership Problem","deck":"As AI starts using enterprise data to answer questions, recommend actions and support workflows, inconsistent definitions of customers, products, revenue, cases or risk stop being reporting annoyances. They become operating constraints on what AI can understand and what the organization can trust it to do.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Data & AI Leadership","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"17 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-is-entering-the-management-layer-leadership-has-to-catch-up","title":"AI Is Entering the Management Layer. Leadership Has to Catch Up.","deck":"AI at work is no longer only about giving employees better tools. As it begins to influence performance, scheduling, training and workforce decisions, leaders need to be much clearer about where technology can support management and where human accountability must remain visible.","kind":"Article","category":"AI Governance","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"15 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-does-not-need-another-dashboard-it-needs-a-management-rhythm","title":"AI Does Not Need Another Dashboard. It Needs a Management Rhythm.","deck":"Many organizations can report AI activity. Fewer have a recurring management discipline that connects spend, adoption, business outcomes and accountability strongly enough to decide what should scale, change or stop.","kind":"Article","category":"Portfolio & Value","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"12 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-changes-the-work-before-performance-systems-catch-up","title":"AI Changes the Work Before Most Performance Systems Catch Up","deck":"Employees are being asked to redesign work with AI while targets, role expectations and management routines still reflect the old process. That mismatch can turn AI adoption into extra work instead of a better operating model.","kind":"Article","category":"AI Adoption","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"08 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"ai-governance-becomes-real-when-accountability-becomes-operational","title":"AI Governance Becomes Real When Accountability Becomes Operational","deck":"Governance should make it clear where AI is used, who owns the consequences, what evidence is required and when intervention is necessary. If those answers are unclear, more policy will not solve the problem.","kind":"Article","category":"AI Governance","read_minutes":6,"published_label":"06 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"when-everyone-has-ai-what-still-creates-competitive-advantage","title":"When Everyone Has AI, What Still Creates Competitive Advantage?","deck":"As AI becomes easier to access, the real difference will come from how companies connect it to business priorities, workflows, people and measurable results.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Portfolio & Value","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"02 Oct 2026"},{"slug":"when-ai-stops-assisting-and-starts-working-the-enterprise-has-a-different-problem","title":"When AI Stops Assisting and Starts Working, the Enterprise Has a Different Problem","deck":"Microsoft’s latest agent announcements made one thing clear to me: we are moving from AI that helps with work to AI that carries work forward, and many companies are not ready for what that changes in practice.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":5,"published_label":"26 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"if-you-wouldnt-ship-an-unsafe-car-why-ship-an-unsafe-ai-model","title":"If You Wouldn’t Ship an Unsafe Car, Why Ship an Unsafe AI Model?","deck":"AI companies these days are calling for stronger safeguards and, in some cases, slower development. I agree — but regulation cannot replace the responsibility of the company deciding whether a model is safe enough to release.","kind":"Point of view","category":"AI Governance","read_minutes":6,"published_label":"25 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"ai-has-too-many-owners-and-thats-why-nobody-owns-the-outcome","title":"AI Has Too Many Owners — and That’s Why Nobody Owns the Outcome","deck":"When responsibility for AI is distributed everywhere, leadership becomes less about control and more about making accountability visible.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Portfolio & Value","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"23 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"the-ai-coe-should-not-become-the-companys-ai-department","title":"The AI CoE Should Not Become the Company’s AI Department","deck":"An AI Center of Excellence should make the enterprise better at owning AI. If every important use case still depends on the center, capability has been concentrated rather than scaled.","kind":"Point of view","category":"AI Operating Model","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"one-ai-adoption-metric-i-dont-trust","title":"One AI Adoption Metric I Don’t Trust","deck":"Active users can tell me that people opened the tool. They cannot tell me that work changed.","kind":"Decision note","category":"AI Adoption","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"why-enterprise-ai-often-stalls-between-pilot-and-scale","title":"Why Enterprise AI Often Stalls Between Pilot and Scale","deck":"A pilot can prove that an AI idea works. It does not prove that the organization is ready to own it, operate it, govern it and create repeatable value from it.","kind":"Point of view","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"the-ai-governance-gate-i-would-never-remove","title":"The AI Governance Gate I Would Never Remove","deck":"AI governance should become lighter when risk is lower. Human accountability should not.","kind":"Decision note","category":"AI Governance","read_minutes":2,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"from-ai-use-case-list-to-investable-portfolio","title":"From AI Use-Case List to Investable Portfolio","deck":"A long list of AI ideas is evidence of demand. It is not evidence of strategy.","kind":"Field note","category":"Portfolio & Value","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"ai-roi-is-often-diagnosed-too-late","title":"AI ROI Is Often Diagnosed Too Late","deck":"If the first serious conversation about value happens after deployment, the problem probably started much earlier.","kind":"Decision note","category":"AI Value","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"when-an-ai-use-case-should-be-stopped","title":"When an AI Use Case Should Be Stopped","deck":"Stopping weak AI work is not portfolio failure. Continuing after the evidence changes often is.","kind":"Field note","category":"AI Portfolio & Value","read_minutes":4,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"},{"slug":"strategy-portfolio-governance-adoption-value","title":"Strategy → Portfolio → Governance → Adoption → Value","deck":"When enterprise AI activity is high but impact is weak, I usually look for a broken link between strategy and value.","kind":"Framework","category":"Enterprise AI","read_minutes":3,"published_label":"17 Sep 2026"}]'''))
